{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0098f537af91e14235dadc780e9896970d1fdc0d3a78534c87711bd95833c5d3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_26cb931cc0172c7a52122495d40db71c46f61af710db12cd9512b6bec3eb1780","slc_cef6ae96253b51b13ec428a7969eed6e75b8cf282673aa6913fda03317e4dc98"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"Documentation states MCP tools must pass three independent checks before use - registry whitelist, a per-service enable toggle, and credential availability - and that of the preset MCP services, thirteen lower-frequency or higher-risk ones default to disabled while a smaller default-enabled set covers web search, maps, and image/video generation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0ae4a2b69195d13ba20965d3d65e1ce101d0141c47f552bec729041418db2cf0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c5f45e8a34b5fd84fa01835d996bd4b5059258c5a9d0e997ff8b5882ad831201"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"Documentation describes a unified authorization pipeline where core tools pass through a Tool Gateway: input normalization, an Operation Analyzer risk/resource check, a system-invariant check, a RUN/SESSION/WORKSPACE grant match or persistent-permission prompt, a pre-execution recheck, and a structured audit of results; high-risk operations are limited to single-use authorization.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e69d18a33e2cdd269485b7c25ae19c899962346c4cd50571a19124cf2675735","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_678274919c5ccb6d3cb596e713bb96c8785e08f7059a3725afbec67d5a646250"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"Documentation states that on a 402 quota-exceeded or 404 model-unavailable response, the system automatically cools that key down for 15 minutes and switches to the next configured API key.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4c2cdb1d021845b04961d62fde11c847001644578f7786be91005ea18d076c1b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1fa85803906e728457a2d1868c1a6e3ff4e1b48f478f0ab96ea9130c4617181d","slc_50d2394da70b19cc16dc220e3cc4f9302a6f00f25cc673caee2a9be347fb2140"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"Documentation states Docker deployment ships the Java backend and a built-in static frontend by default in one container, with an optional managed Python service included in the image but not started, and not exposing a port, unless explicitly enabled via environment variables or a compose override.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7977a466349508f09e7091b0507a2e17bbcdbd95b8a97eddd92fa07842ea42e6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_11c48d9fa98670e1302f1b1b147e2763fdb7d3e0e0ca7e1404b5b4eeb96986fd","slc_9449ee6950c904a710360caa3b7c491917bd044baa08a16025db9adcc998d329"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"Documentation describes a three-tier architecture: a Java 21/Spring Boot backend handling core orchestration, LLM routing, and the authorization gateway; a React/TypeScript frontend for the interactive UI; and an optional Python/FastAPI service for code analysis and MCP bridging.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7a1621f582660cf19c0e826b30472346b732baa66e3e26df82507c75f9bde81c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c5f45e8a34b5fd84fa01835d996bd4b5059258c5a9d0e997ff8b5882ad831201"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"Documentation states that referencing a local file when connected directly adds only its path to the prompt without uploading content, but doing so over a remote or proxied connection instead uploads the file as a permanent public OSS object and requires OSS to be configured first.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a70e6822e385ce9d3c5eb8b2c4eb30ae29da878f792680000a6bec228c9a9711","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e43a92e4a827e86f5eaf671dc1a5f872e2f1a7fc174e1f6235f8152267593329"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"The README describes ZhikunCode as an open-source AI programming assistant deployed once and controllable entirely from a browser, with multi-agent collaboration, Docker self-hosting, direct connections to domestic Chinese LLM providers, and what it calls a deep security architecture.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cf1be386b8c04cdab5abe264204053ccdc0b441eafeab0e42fb591740c28da0c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_51d32fb8605cb6a87e3d643ff53ed4258dba5948707d48e8a346d7e0157065d4"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"The README describes a six-level context-compression cascade (Snip, MicroCompact, ContextCollapse, AutoCompact, CollapseDrain, ReactiveCompact) intended to keep sessions within the context window, with a documented two-stage CollapseDrain/ReactiveCompact recovery path for large sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e7e501fd2cdf4edbfe1ee3f688e49ebd796e05d2c59bd3a3b60320143e8732b4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c5f45e8a34b5fd84fa01835d996bd4b5059258c5a9d0e997ff8b5882ad831201"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"The README lists three multi-agent collaboration modes: Team for fixed role division, Swarm for dynamic negotiation, and SubAgent for master/subordinate delegation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f3b98eebe4bd0845a84c2740ed886384d63b8e37cd795aa140037cf7d63174f2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_60a7457383366ceb142cdb5bca7375417c2fc7039dec3f5631b31318af793b95","slc_c64945225b8b99fe18b87da5a9d12753072237f779fe3e92c92f7d18c2ad2867"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"The README reports ZhikunCode completed the SWE-bench Lite benchmark (300 instances, pass@1) against an official harness, with a resolve rate of 168/300 (56.0%) and a patch-generation rate of 284/300 (94.7%), and states the evaluation artifacts are open-sourced for third-party reproduction.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f84a0ca9b1f834a385ec9ce087d194537dd0511f1fc07ceb23772700fd4c96c6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"zhikunqingtao/zhikuncode@931a9beebf21 snapshot c7992362e1b91e4b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d75fff3af0b8cd269586f5e4f9b27fde3a115a4641ce892641b5d6ac4c7e0b6d"],"source_ids":["src_880bb598b9ba516fac20874f2d4250e7"],"text":"A documented provider table lists direct connections to DashScope (Qianwen, the default), DeepSeek, Moonshot (Kimi), Zhipu GLM, and MiniMax as domestic options, plus OpenAI (requiring external network access) and a fully offline local Ollama option.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T05:00:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_02fe12f98ea947bc912da97c8dca2ebc"}
